{
  "category": "Coral Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "It continuously sheds and grows. The tip of its head is prized as a treasure for its beauty.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a south sea nation, the people live in communi ties that are built on groups of these POKéMON.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "The points on its head absorb nutrients from clean water. They cannot survive in polluted water.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "CORSOLA’s branches glitter very beautifully in seven colors when they catch sunlight. If any branch breaks off, this POKéMON grows it back in just one night.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Clusters of CORSOLA congregate in warm seas where they serve as ideal hiding places for smaller POKéMON. When the water temperature falls, this POKéMON migrates to the southern seas.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "CORSOLA live in warm southern seas. If the sea becomes polluted, the beautiful coral stalks become discolored and crumble away in tatters.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a south sea nation, the people live in communities that are built on groups of these POKéMON.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "It continuously sheds and grows. The tip of its head is prized as a treasure for its beauty.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "Many live in the clean seas of the south. They apparently can’t live in polluted waters.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "Many live in the clean seas of the south. They apparently can’t live in polluted waters.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "Many live in the clean seas of the south. They apparently can’t live in polluted waters.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "It continuously sheds and grows. The tip of its head is prized as a treasure because of its beauty.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a south-sea nation, the people live in communities that are built on groups of these Pokémon.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "Many live in the clean seas of the south. They apparently can’t live in polluted waters.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "Many live in the clean seas of the south. They apparently can’t live in polluted waters.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "They prefer unpolluted southern seas. Their coral branches lose their color and deteriorate in dirty water.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "They prefer unpolluted southern seas. Their coral branches lose their color and deteriorate in dirty water.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "It continuously sheds and grows. The tip of its head is prized as a treasure because of its beauty.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "They prefer unpolluted southern seas. Their coral branches lose their color and deteriorate in dirty water.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Corsola’s branches glitter very beautifully in seven colors when they catch sunlight. If any branch breaks off, this Pokémon grows it back in just one night.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Clusters of Corsola congregate in warm seas where they serve as ideal hiding places for smaller Pokémon. When the water temperature falls, this Pokémon migrates to the southern seas.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Coral branches grow from its head. They break off quite easily, but they grow back in about three days.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pursued by Mareanie for the branches on its head, this Pokémon will sometimes snap its own branches off as a diversion while it escapes.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "The pink of Corsola that live in Alola is deep and vibrant, thanks to seas filled with nutrition.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "In Alola, where their natural enemies Mareanie are plentiful, many Corsola have stubby branches on their heads.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It will regrow any branches that break off its head. People keep particularly beautiful Corsola branches as charms to promote safe childbirth.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "These Pokémon live in warm seas. In prehistoric times, many lived in the oceans around the Galar region as well.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
